WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:20.609 --> 00:00:24.320
Do you ever imagine your own funeral?

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:25.649
I do.

00:00:25.649 --> 00:00:26.719
In fact,

00:00:26.719 --> 00:00:29.519
it may be something I think about a little bit
too much,

00:00:29.519 --> 00:00:32.810
given my age and health and happiness.

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:38.200
But as someone with an interest in liturgy and an inclination towards self-reflection,

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.710
imagining and even planning my own funeral

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:43.260
is a fascinating possibility.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.300
Will prayers that I have written be used?

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.560
Will there be liturgical dance?

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:49.900
What photos will surface?

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.060
Who will attend?

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:53.470
Who will speak?

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:55.090
And most importantly,

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:58.620
what will they say?

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:02.850
I hope they will say that I loved.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.830
They may speak about my academic. Not irritable or resentful.

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:11.470
It does not rejoice in wrongdoing but rejoices in the truth.

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:15.380
Love bears all things, believes all things, hopes 

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:17.280
all things. Love

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:21.710
the never ends.

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:27.210
We could bask in the beauty of Paul's ode to love all day.

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:31.220
This is an incredibly evocative description
of love.

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:34.810
And for many of us it brings to mind romantic
love.

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:37.689
This passage is often read at weddings.

00:01:37.689 --> 00:01:40.880
And with February 14th only two weeks
away,

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:44.870
we are surrounded by eternal devotion

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:48.500
declared on candy hearts, shop windows full of pink, pre-packaged
romance, and

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:52.240
invitations to speed dating at Gypsy.

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:55.760
But Paul is writing about more than romantic

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:58.909
love. He is writing about the love of a whole community.

00:01:58.909 --> 00:02:03.180
A community composed of people very different
from one another,

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:04.170
poor and rich,

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:05.920
female and male,

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:07.720
liberal and conservative,

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:11.459
politically, socially, and theologically.

00:02:11.459 --> 00:02:16.279
And Paul is exhorting them all to love one another.

00:02:16.279 --> 00:02:20.609
When we listen to this description of love with this context in 

00:02:20.609 --> 00:02:25.079
mind, we realize how difficult and demanding real love is.

00:02:25.079 --> 00:02:26.729
Love is

00:02:26.729 --> 00:02:28.279
patient. Love is kind.

00:02:28.279 --> 00:02:32.109
Love is not envious, boastful, arrogant or rude.

00:02:32.109 --> 00:02:34.729
Love does not insist on its own way.

00:02:34.729 --> 00:02:37.129
Love is not irritable or resentful.

00:02:37.129 --> 00:02:41.559
Love does not rejoice in wrongdoing, but rejoices in the truth.

00:02:41.559 --> 00:02:43.359
Love bears all

00:02:43.359 --> 00:02:48.309
things, believes all things, hopes all things, endures all

00:02:48.309 --> 00:02:51.809
things. Love never ends. Is there no escape?

00:02:51.809 --> 00:02:56.059
Suddenly love has become a lot more challenging.

00:02:56.059 --> 00:02:59.109
Suddenly love is not a warm fuzzy feeling,

00:02:59.109 --> 00:03:02.739
or even a deep abiding commitment.

00:03:02.739 --> 00:03:05.350
Suddenly love is about everything we do,

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:07.699
everything we think, everything we feel,

00:03:07.699 --> 00:03:12.559
our attitudes, our habits, our actions, our beliefs, our hopes.

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:16.999
Love is demanded in every aspect of our lives.

00:03:16.999 --> 00:03:20.299
And love is not only about one romantic partner,

00:03:20.299 --> 00:03:22.279
but about everyone,

00:03:22.279 --> 00:03:23.199
friends,

00:03:23.199 --> 00:03:24.319
family,

00:03:24.319 --> 00:03:25.109
enemies,

00:03:25.109 --> 00:03:29.389
the people we don't even know exist.

00:03:29.389 --> 00:03:33.789
This radical love described by Paul is mysterious.

00:03:33.789 --> 00:03:36.159
We can only know it in part.

00:03:36.159 --> 00:03:39.459
We can only see it through a mirror dimly.

00:03:39.459 --> 00:03:44.419
We can only glimpse shadowy reflections
of this love,

00:03:44.419 --> 00:03:50.619
but these shadowy reflections are the most important thing in the world.

00:03:50.619 --> 00:03:54.629
We can glimpse this live by looking at the people in our

00:03:54.629 --> 00:03:58.229
lives and in our faith traditions who embody love.

00:03:58.229 --> 00:03:59.959
We

00:03:59.959 --> 00:04:05.789
can glimpse this love by telling the real love stories.

00:04:05.789 --> 00:04:09.019
My former pastor and colleague Joel

00:04:09.019 --> 00:04:14.279
showed me what it means to love in the most mundane and ordinary moments.

00:04:14.279 --> 00:04:17.150
Joel took time with each person he encountered

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:20.169
to make that person feel like they mattered -

00:04:20.169 --> 00:04:22.039
the custodian at church,

00:04:22.039 --> 00:04:24.229
the photographer at the reception,

00:04:24.229 --> 00:04:26.629
the other passenger in the elevator,

00:04:26.629 --> 00:04:29.909
the quiet youth on the fringes of the church youth group,

00:04:29.909 --> 00:04:33.909
and the rebel who everyone else had already
given up on.

00:04:33.909 --> 00:04:35.580
Joel was often late.

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:39.050
And I will admit that people who are late normally really annoy me,

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:42.790
but with Joel, it didn't bother me quite as much,

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:46.620
because I suspected that he was late because he had stopped 

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:47.789
to listen to someone

00:04:47.789 --> 00:04:53.539
who needed to talk or taking that extra moment to acknowledge that the service worker was a person, not a machine.

00:04:53.539 --> 00:04:55.129
Love is patient,

00:04:55.129 --> 00:04:57.080
love is kind.

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:59.039
Love takes time for people

00:04:59.039 --> 00:05:01.699
no matter what.

00:05:01.699 --> 00:05:04.190
Who has shown you love that is patient

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:10.389
and kind?

00:05:10.389 --> 00:05:12.620
Jesus returned to his

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:16.630
hometown, stood up in front of the religious community that raised him

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:18.439
and declared,  "I am the fulfillment of Scripture.

00:05:18.439 --> 00:05:20.759
I am the Messiah."

00:05:20.759 --> 00:05:24.539
We heard about this in the glorious gospel
reading last week

00:05:24.539 --> 00:05:27.310
and this week we heard the results.

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:30.260
Members of jesus community ran him out of town

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:32.699
and threatened to throw him off a cliff.

00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:36.190
This is the good news of the gospel.

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:38.759
Love is about speaking the truth,

00:05:38.759 --> 00:05:41.039
even when it's risky.

00:05:41.039 --> 00:05:45.330
Love is about saying the things that you just
aren't supposed to say.

00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:49.239
Love is not always about being nice.

00:05:49.239 --> 00:05:51.529
Love rejoices in the truth,

00:05:51.529 --> 00:05:53.179
even the hard truth

00:05:53.179 --> 00:05:56.289
no matter what.

00:05:56.289 --> 00:06:03.289
Who has given you a glimpse of love that rejoices
in the truth?

00:06:07.149 --> 00:06:09.259
This community at University Church

00:06:09.259 --> 00:06:12.139
has also taught me about love.

00:06:12.139 --> 00:06:16.330
You are some of the most talented and impressive
people I have ever met.

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:21.180
I tremble at the thought of your resumes.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:25.550
And soon many of you will have a label permanently attached to your name

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:28.199
that will declare to the world you are exceptional.

00:06:28.199 --> 00:06:29.759
At the same time

00:06:29.759 --> 00:06:33.900
you have shown me what it means to love in
ways that are not boastful or 

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:35.560
arrogant or rude.

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:38.129
Some of you have shown love through the questions you ask

00:06:38.129 --> 00:06:41.089
and your readiness to learn.

00:06:41.089 --> 00:06:44.610
Some of you have love through your openness
to trying new things,

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:47.840
even things you might not be good at.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:50.649
Some of you have shown love through your willingness

00:06:50.649 --> 00:06:55.509
to help out with no expectation of recognition or reward.

00:06:55.509 --> 00:06:59.229
Love is not boastful or arrogant or rude.

00:06:59.229 --> 00:07:00.650
Love is

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:04.179
humble no matter what you have accomplished.

00:07:04.179 --> 00:07:11.179
Who has given you a glimpse of humble love?

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:19.209
My grandma and grandpa were married in 1942.

00:07:19.209 --> 00:07:23.579
I remember the huge party celebrating their
50th wedding anniversary in

00:07:23.579 --> 00:07:24.419
1992.

00:07:24.419 --> 00:07:30.789
I had a brand new pink dress and helped to decorate their cars with colorful flowers and streamers.

00:07:30.789 --> 00:07:35.780
Over the following 10 years my grandfather's
health began to fail.

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:40.279
My grandparents moved out of their house and into a condo.

00:07:40.279 --> 00:07:44.590
Eventually my grandfather moved into the nursing
home next door.

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:50.249
My Grandfather, my grandmother walked over
every day to visit him.

00:07:50.249 --> 00:07:54.919
When my grandparents celebrated their 61st
wedding anniversary in 

00:07:54.919 --> 00:07:56.470
2003,

00:07:56.470 --> 00:08:00.679
both my grandmother and grandfather were very
ill.

00:08:00.679 --> 00:08:02.849
The night before my grandmother died

00:08:02.849 --> 00:08:07.679
she had a lucid moment and a nurse recorded her words.

00:08:07.679 --> 00:08:11.219
She spoke of her love for her children and
grandchildren

00:08:11.219 --> 00:08:13.569
and of her love for her husband,

00:08:13.569 --> 00:08:17.509
even though he could no longer read the newspaper.

00:08:17.509 --> 00:08:18.430
At first

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:21.099
I found these last words tragic.

00:08:21.099 --> 00:08:25.859
My grandmother's final thoughts of my grandfather
were about how he was no longer the man

00:08:25.859 --> 00:08:28.969
he used to be.

00:08:28.969 --> 00:08:31.749
Now I hear it differently.

00:08:31.749 --> 00:08:36.190
My grandmother's last words were about how much she loved my grandfather

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:36.810
despite

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:42.710
and because he was no longer the man she had
married 61 years before.

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:44.740
Within a week of my grandmother's death,

00:08:44.740 --> 00:08:47.500
my grandfather also passed away.

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:52.230
After more than six decades, how could they
be apart?

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:54.480
Love endures.

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:57.720
Love survives challenge and change

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:00.510
no matter what

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:07.510
Who has given you a glimpse of love that
endures?

00:09:11.220 --> 00:09:12.500
Dirk Willams

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:14.690
was one of my forebears in 

00:09:14.690 --> 00:09:18.010
faith in the Mennonite faith tradition.

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:22.330
He was a sixteenth-century church leader
in the Netherlands who was imprisoned on account

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:25.360
of his beliefs.

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:28.730
After being imprisoned for a year Dirk escaped.

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:32.360
He was pursued across a frozen river by a prison
guard

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:36.180
and after he had safely reached the far bank
he heard a loud crack

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:37.760
behind him.

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:42.790
The ice had broken and the guard had fallen
through into the frigid water.

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:45.740
Dirk hesitated for only a second

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:47.580
before turning around,

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:49.430
inching across the ice,

00:09:49.430 --> 00:09:53.120
and extending his hands to his captor.

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:55.830
He pulled the guard safely to shore.

00:09:55.830 --> 00:09:58.210
And the guard wanted to let Dirk go,

00:09:58.210 --> 00:10:03.050
but his supervisor arrived and called out to
him to hold Dirk.

00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:05.620
The guard returned Dirk to prison

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:10.250
and he was burned at the stake several months
later.

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:12.670
Dirk Willams died for

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:17.300
his faith, a faith that taught him that the lives of his enemies were worth saving,

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:21.350
even at the cost of his own life.

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:25.080
Love does not insist on its own way.

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:27.370
Love puts the other person first

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:29.970
no matter what.

00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:32.499
Who has given you a glimpse of

00:10:32.499 --> 00:10:39.499
love that does not insist on its own way?

00:10:40.730 --> 00:10:42.820
After hearing these

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:47.110
stories, how can I even hope to embody a fraction of
the love lived out by these individuals

00:10:47.110 --> 00:10:48.870
and communities&gt;

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:54.800
How could I presume to suggest that at my funeral
people would celebrate that I loved?

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:57.520
I am overwhelmed by my own failure to love

00:10:57.520 --> 00:11:03.890
and by a world that so often seems so inhospitable to love.

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:05.500
And then I remember

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:09.140
that love is not all about me.

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:11.339
Sometimes it may feel like it's all about me -

00:11:11.339 --> 00:11:15.380
my feelings, my thoughts, my desires, my actions.

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:19.170
But love is not all about me.

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:23.030
At other times it feels like love is all about other people,

00:11:23.030 --> 00:11:28.030
about putting the feelings, thoughts, desires, and actions of others first.

00:11:28.030 --> 00:11:32.340
But love is not all about other people either.

00:11:32.340 --> 00:11:34.990
Love is all about God.

00:11:34.990 --> 00:11:38.600
Love is all about God being all about everyone.

00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:43.350
It is about God loving other people and God loving me and

00:11:43.350 --> 00:11:47.370
especially about God bringing you and me and us and them together.

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:50.550
Because love is all about God being all about

00:11:50.550 --> 00:11:53.660
everyone, love can never be separated from justice 

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:58.020
or forgiveness.

00:11:58.020 --> 00:12:01.930
Regardless of what I believe in this moment
about God and whether

00:12:01.930 --> 00:12:02.989
God exists,

00:12:02.989 --> 00:12:05.430
or is powerful or is good, love is still about God.

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:10.110
Love is something beyond and within us, something that moves us towards one another,

00:12:10.110 --> 00:12:14.750
something that moves us towards our most honest selves.

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:16.110
This kind of God,

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:19.870
this kind of love is something to celebrate.

00:12:19.870 --> 00:12:24.280
God's love revealed in human love is something to celebrate.

00:12:24.280 --> 00:12:28.189
So we celebrate the love of Joel and Jesus

00:12:28.189 --> 00:12:30.289
and University Church and my grandparents and

00:12:30.289 --> 00:12:35.070
Dirk and all of the other people who have given us
glimpses of God's love.

00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:38.390
We celebrate love that is patient and kind,

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:40.680
love that rejoices in the truth,

00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:42.279
love that is humble,

00:12:42.279 --> 00:12:48.439
love that endures, love that does not insist on its own way, love that bears

00:12:48.439 --> 00:12:51.560
all things, believes all things, hopes all things,

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:54.300
love that never ends.

00:12:54.300 --> 00:13:00.580
We celebrate God's love reflected in human love in every moment of life,

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:03.130
love present when sperm meets egg,

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:06.360
when lungs meet air,

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:13.360
when parents meet child, when child meets friends, when youth meet enemies,  when people meet passions, when partner meets

00:13:13.420 --> 00:13:14.100
partner,

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:18.320
when age meets wisdom,

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:21.390
when body meets earth,

00:13:21.390 --> 00:13:24.720
when spirit meets spirit.

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:26.540
Love never ends.

00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:31.090
This is the type of love I hope friends and family will celebrate at my funeral.

00:13:31.090 --> 00:13:36.170
This is the type of love I hope to celebrate in every moment of my life.

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:41.290
This is the type of love I hope our life together can celebrate.

00:13:41.290 --> 00:13:44.450
God is this love. This is God's love. Amen.

